      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- The Library [zone=751]\n**Who:**\n- Tarlyn Caelith [npc=36186]\nRating:\n0/5**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\n(Average from 5 ratings)\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 90\n**Maximum Level:** | 90\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Experience\n- Faction\n- Loot\n- Money\n**Time Limit:** | 06:00:00\n**Success Lockout Timer**: 06:00:00\n**Factions Raised:**\n- Dream Delvers +?\n**Factions Lowered:**\n**Quest Items:**\n- Ancient Spellbook [item=91144]\n- Old Spell Codex [item=90269]\n- Unusual Tome [item=90294]\n- Worn Book [item=90478]\n**Related Zones:**\n- The Library: A Moment of Clarity [zone=768]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Sage Weldan [npc=36559]\n- Tarlyn Caelith [npc=38025]\n- an ornate chest - A Moment of Clarity [npc=36558]\n**Era:** | !House of Thule\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Group\n**Min. # of Players:** | 3\n**Max. # of Players:** | 6\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Wed Nov 3 19:14:03 2010\nModified: Sat Sep 28 07:21:33 2024 | | _This is a non-progression group mission (3-6 players) that begins with Tarlyn Caelith in the Library. He is found at location 55, 285, -3 (in the hallway west of the room with the various scholars)._\n_There are no pre-requisites for requesting this task._\n_Note: This is a Tier 4 difficulty task, meaning mob difficulty will be along the same lines as Morell's Castle and Sanctum Somnium._\nYou say, 'Hail, Tarlyn Caelith'\nTarlyn Caelith says 'Please tell me you are not here to try to kill me. I'm getting quite sick of running around in this library. At least I'm having better luck than that Kintorom fellow. Still, even though I'm [close], I still need more time!'\nYou say, 'How close?'\nTarlyn Caelith says 'Very close! To finding the answers. About what is [wrong]. I'm not like the others. I know something is wrong here. Though I distinctly remember finding this library, I believe my memory, and almost everything about this place is again, for lack of a better word, [wrong].'\nYou say, 'Wrong?'\nTarlyn Caelith says 'Yes. In fact, I think you know more about this than anyone else here. Still, I'm afraid my moment of clarity won't last too long. I'll need to act fast. There is a spellbook here in this library. I saw it, I almost had it, but one of those strange librarians took it and almost killed me. We must [acquire] it!'\nYou say, 'Yes, we must acquire it...'\nTarlyn Caelith says 'I'm glad to see you agree. Let me know when you are [prepared]. I warn you, this will become violent, and I am not going to be of much use to you in a fight. However, I will be able to use that book once we find it.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'A Moment of Clarity'.\nYou say, 'We're prepared!'\nTarlyn Caelith says 'Excellent. This way. We'll return to the first floor and start there.'\nLOADING, PLEASE WAIT...\nYou have entered The Library.\n\n---\n\n_Summary: You'll have to find Unusual Tomes, Old Spell Codices, and Worn Books (groundspawns you'll find as you make your way upstairs); and kill listless librarians, weary assistants, and finally, Sage Weldan._\n_Mobs in this zone are mostly yellow /cons to Level 90 and mostly melee._\nSearch the entrance for books 0/1 (The Library)\nSearch the ground floor for books 0/1 (The Library)\nSearch the mid-floor library for books 0/1 (The Library)\nSearch the winding stairwell for books 0/1 (The Library)\nSearch the top floor for books 0/1 (The Library)\nDeliver any unusual tomes found to Tarlyn 0/3 (The Library)\nDeliver any worn books found to Tarlyn 0/3 (The Library)\nDeliver any old spell codices found to Tarlyn 0/3 (The Library)\nTarlyn Caelith says 'You've done well, my friend. These books will prove useful, but they aren't exactly the ones I'm looking for.'\nDefeat any librarians that interfere 0/10 (The Library)\nDefeat any assistants that interfere 0/8 (The Library)\nObtain information from Sage Weldan 0/1 (The Library)\nSage Weldan eyes you with disdain and runs in for the attack!\n_Sage Weldan's DPS output is only slightly higher than that of the trash mobs in the zone. He has ~1.1 million hitpoints and casts the spells \"Delusion Visage I\" and \"Shadow Lore\":_\nDelusion Visage I: PB AE 30', Chromatic (-700)\n1: Decrease Movement by 80%\nShadow Lore: PB AE 200', Magic (-650)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 11900\n2: Decrease Mana by 2380\nSage Weldan has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\nSage Weldan's corpse gasps for air, choking out one final breath.\nObtain the ancient spellbook from Sage Weldan 0/1 (The Library)\nReturn the ancient spellbook to Tarlyn Caelith 0/1 (The Library)\nSpeak to Tarlyn Caelith 0/1 (The Library)\nYou say, 'Hail, Tarlyn Caelith'\nTarlyn Caelith says 'I knew you could do it! This is just the book I was looking for. I hope Sage Weldan didn't give you too much trouble? This place is mad. Thank you friend. With your help, I might be able to end this nightmare. At least, I hope so. I'll need some time to study. Don't let me keep you!'\nTake your reward from the chest 0/1 (The Library)\nWith your aid, Tarlyn Caelith obtained the book of magic he was looking for. However, it is unclear if he will remember what has transpired, or be lucid enough to decipher the text to assist some of the trapped dreamers. You had best continue your efforts in other areas while he studies the text.\n\n---\n\n_Task rewards:_\n315 platinum\nExperience\nFaction with Dream Delvers\n80 Dream Motes [item=90255]\n_Known Chest Loot [npc=36558] (1 item + 1 spell per task):_\nBielaisk's Cape\nConjurer's Orb\nDream Destroyer's Hand\nGuardian's Greaves\nKnight Captain's Shield\nMace of Dark Dreams\nMalleable Core of the Guardian\nNesalie's Spell Gem\nQuentin's Outfit\nShadow Warden's Rapier\nMinor Nebulous Dream Fragment\nLesser Nebulous Dream Fragment\nMedian Nebulous Dream Fragment\nGreater Nebulous Dream Fragment\nGlowing Nebulous Dream Fragment\n- Dream Mote [item=90255]",
